nstructs backward and forward shape, Wronskian, Gaussian-tail and derivative premises and calls gaussian_shape_coercivity. That theorem integrates on Ioi 0, proves zero endpoint flux and reflects. This is an authored proof-body correspondence, not an extracted dependency or fresh Lean acceptance. The whole-line integrated_coercivity_of_flux helper is not this application.","citation_ids":["support-r2-13-finite-density-call","full_support_origin_coercivity"],"evidence_ids":["R2-13-SUP-001"],"id":"support.source_finite_density_coercivity","kind":"claim","label":"Concrete finite-data half-line coercivity application","locator":"Density/FiniteDensity.lean:111–188","source_id":"support-r2-13-finite-density","statement":"For c:N→NNReal strictly positive at every index, monotone and bounded above by M, h:NNReal with h>0, and natural indices 0<i≤N, put r(x)=c(i)*deriv(backwardBoundary c h (softAbs M) N i)(x). Then (1/1000) times the finiteDensity-weighted integral of quarticMoment r is at most the corresponding integral of coercivePolynomial r. The same inequality holds as a finite-feedback diffusion expectation after finite_density_identity.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.source_finite_density_coercivity","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"citations","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.integrated_coercivity","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.integrated_coercivity%22%2C%22support.source_finite_density_coercivity%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","kind":"cites","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.integrated_coercivity%22%2C%22support.source_finite_density_coercivity%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","semantic_class":"citation_reference","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/sup